<article class="env-remark" id="0FQR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FQR">Remark <span data-tag="0FQR">22.30.2</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $(A, \text{d})$ and $(B, \text{d})$ be differential graded algebras over $R$. Let $N$ be a differential graded $(A, B)$-bimodule. Let $N'$ be a right differential graded $B$-module. Then for every $k \in \mathbf{Z}$ there is an isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\text{Mod}^{gr}_ B}(N, N')[k] \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\text{Mod}^{gr}_ B}(N, N'[k])  \]
</div>
  <p> of right differential graded $A$-modules defined without the intervention of signs, see More on Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/0FNG" data-tag="0FNG">15.74</a>. </p>
</article>